",\n        \"A legal producer-to-consumer schedule distinguishing nonvoter support from pending voter callbacks.\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 3,\n      \"trigger_rationale\": \"Developer documentation identifies voters as the verification support participants; quorumSize computes their majority. Registration and notification instead cover all replication peers. A bounded local eligibility comparison can observe whether a nonvoter acknowledgment increments that count; it need not infer a global stale read or wait for a numeric progress deadline.\"\n    },\n    \"status\": \"escalated\",\n    \"parent_candidate_id\": null,\n    \"fork_reason\": \"\",\n    \"stop_reason\": \"Ground the selected local participant-eligibility obligation using implementation-specific developer documentation and API purpose. Formal execution will separately establish whether nonvoter acknowledgments affect the count.\",\n    \"resume_conditions\": [],\n    \"obligation_id\": \"claim-verify-voter-eligibility\",\n    \"result_claim_ids\": [],\n    \"open_issue_ids\": [],\n    \"executions\": [],\n    \"record\": {\n      \"path\": \"state.json\",\n      \"collection\": \"question_candidates\",\n      \"match\": {\n        \"id\": \"1d5c5370f370484aac627d6b65c29f38\"\n      }\n    }\n  }\n]\nunits [\n  {\n    \"id\": \"unit-claim-verify-voter-eligibility\",\n    \"candidate_id\": \"1d5c5370f370484aac627d6b65c29f38\",\n    \"obligation_ids\": [\n      \"claim-verify-voter-eligibility\"\n    ],\n    \"binding_ids\": [\n      \"bind-verify-registration\",\n      \"bind-verify-notification\",\n      \"bind-verify-tally\"\n    ],\n    \"relation_ids\": [],\n    \"scope\": {\n      \"description\": \"Participant eligibility in the per-request VerifyLeader quorum tally, with an unchanged mixed voter/nonvoter configuration and no concurrent leadership/configuration transition during the measured accounting step.\",\n      \"assumptions\": [\n        \"Correct peer identities and suffrage; non-By